; a comment at the end of a line of a statement that continues on the next line ends at its line:
; the lines of a statement were joined first, so the comment swallowed the rest ("unexpected end
; of file") -- and Kurt's own output of a multi-row matrix, with the reason as such a comment,
; couldn't be pasted back as source (found 2026-10-09)
load prop
bool A, B
use (A        ; a comment inside the statement
  implies B)  ; and one at its end
use A
B

load matrix
calc on
const M
use M = [[1, 2],                          ; 5 without proof
         [3, 4]]
M = [[1, 2],                              ; the output of Kurt, pasted
     [3, 4]]
